\caption{
Logical error rate per round of syndrome extraction for the studied layouts under the circuit-level noise model. A shot is counted as a logical failure if at least one of the twelve tracked logical observables is decoded incorrectly. We first estimate the experiment-level probability \(p_{\mathrm{any}}\) of one or more logical failures over \(R\) syndrome extraction rounds, then report the equivalent per-round rate \(p_{\mathrm{any,round}} = 1 - (1-p_{\mathrm{any}})^{1/R}\). We include 95\(\%\) Wilson confidence intervals. 
